comment.narrative:
The FEEP projects builds upon previous PSD interventions and previous initiatives of teh Dutch embassy in Maputo: 

In 2017,  the embassy empowered 500 female entrepreneurs working in formal and informal sectors in projects stimulating women to start their own business and job creation. Two pilot projects have been implemented by the embassy through the PSD Toolkit program (in 2017-2018) to offer female entrepreneurs training in business development, mentoring and networking opportunities to grasp new business opportunities. These efforts created opportunities for female entrepreneurs to expose their businesses, be in a supportive environment and have the opportunity to be engaged in global initiatives, such as the “The Women in Business Global Mentoring Program” and being featured in an international magazine. Moreover, over the years, the embassy has played an increasingly active role in the emerging Maputo entrepreneurship ecosystem and has supported a number of gender-smart entrepreneurship development initiatives implemented by ideialab, including:
?	The pilot for Business M+, for early-stage women entrepreneurs who need structure &/ formalisation to achieve growth (ideialab has since rolled out this program in several provinces); 
?	Three cohorts of Femtech: an acceleration program for women entrepreneurs with established businesses ready for growth, which is proposed under this Project;
?	The Orange Corners Maputo incubation program and space for young aspiring entrepreneurs to take their idea to startup (which since the program´s digital migration because of COVID-19 has reached entrepreneurs country-wide); 

The FEEP project continued to grow the skills and capacity along the entrepreneurship journey of graduates coming out of Business M+ and the Orange Corners Maputo incubation program (which targeted women entrepreneurs the pre-idea, idea and startup phase) now to structure, grow and scale their businesses. The FEEP project recahed female owned businesses that were not reached (geographically and s
